---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import { currentSite } from '../../data/sites.mjs';
import { BRAND } from '../../data/brand.mjs';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema.mjs';

/*
 * TODO: LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH
 *
 * This is a standard template written to describe what the site actually does.
 * It has not been reviewed by an attorney. Before any domain goes live it needs
 * a lawyer to confirm the disclosures against the states we operate in and
 * against how CRMX and Make.com actually store and process submissions.
 *
 * Known items for that review:
 *   - Whether any state we operate in requires additional notice for lead data.
 *   - Retention period. The wording below is deliberately non-committal.
 *   - Whether a "do not sell my personal information" notice is required.
 */

const site = currentSite();
const updated = 'July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${BRAND.name} collects, uses, and protects the information you send through this site.`}
  path="/privacy"
  schemas={[
    breadcrumbSchema(site, [
      { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { label: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <div class="page section">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <Prose>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you fill out a form on this site, we collect what you type into it:
        your name, phone number, email address, and the details you give us about
        your property. We do not ask for a Social Security number, a bank
        account, or any payment information, and you should never send those to
        us.
      </p>
      <p>
        Like most websites, our hosting provider records basic technical
        information such as the type of device and browser used to load a page.
        We do not use this to identify you.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>
        We use what you send us for two purposes. First, to evaluate whether
        your property fits what we are looking for. Second, to contact you about
        it. That is the whole list.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your information. We do not trade it, and we do not
        provide it to anyone marketing unrelated products to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do use outside services to run our business, including a customer
        relationship system that stores contact records and an email provider
        that delivers our messages. Those companies process information on our
        behalf and are not permitted to use it for their own purposes. If we
        move toward a transaction on your property, we may need to share
        relevant details with parties directly involved in that transaction,
        such as a title company or an attorney.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may also disclose information where the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep property and contact records for as long as they are useful to
        the work described above. If you want your information removed, email us
        and we will remove it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not use advertising cookies and does not track you across
        other websites. If we add analytics later, this page will be updated
        before we do.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to
        delete it. Email <a href={`mailto:${BRAND.email}`}>{BRAND.email}</a> and
        we will take care of it. You can also ask us to stop contacting you at
        any time, and we will.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is meant for adults who own or manage land. It is not directed
        at children and we do not knowingly collect information from them.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top of this
        page.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can go to
        <a href={`mailto:${BRAND.email}`}>{BRAND.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</Base>
